# Copy to .dev.vars for `wrangler dev`. Never commit .dev.vars.
# Values here override the production vars in wrangler.jsonc.

# --- Option A: no sign-in at all (quickest). Honoured only while BETTER_AUTH_SECRET is unset.
# Power mode acts as the `default` account and may use the server keys below; Learn mode
# (/learn/) acts as `default_simple`. Credit (Option C) is on `default_simple` for both.
DEV_ALLOW_NO_AUTH=true

# --- Option B: real sign-in, locally. Comment out DEV_ALLOW_NO_AUTH above and fill these in.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=            # openssl rand -base64 32
# Anyone can sign up. Signed-in users never get the server keys below: power mode is bring-your-own-key.
# Your own user id (the Account ID in the account menu once signed in) opens the admin app at /admin/.
# Comma-separated for several. Under Option A the dev bypass is always admin.
# ADMIN_USER_IDS=
# Magic links are printed to the wrangler console instead of emailed (localhost only):
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=log
# Cloudflare's Turnstile test keys (always pass):
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# Optional OAuth apps (callback URLs: http://localhost:8787/api/auth/callback/google and .../github):
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# To send real email instead: EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend, RESEND_API_KEY=re_..., EMAIL_FROM=...

# Server-side provider keys: used only by the dev bypass (Option A), never for signed-in users.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# Enables bring-your-own-key (users paste their own provider key in the UI). 32 random bytes, base64:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=

# --- The built-in provider on credit, and the membership, in both apps. See README "Membership, credit and billing".
# Without these, both apps run only on each user's own keys (needs KEY_ENCRYPTION_SECRET).
# OpenRouter key that the built-in provider `tangent` spends (Learn's "Use Tangent credit", power's
# "Tangent credit"; give it a small credit limit). No fallback to OPENROUTER_API_KEY:
# OPENROUTER_SIMPLE_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# Payments: Polar's sandbox (https://sandbox.polar.sh; test card 4242 4242 4242 4242). Both secrets
# must be set for billing (and for the built-in provider to be offered at all). wrangler.jsonc says
# POLAR_SERVER=production, so set the sandbox here:
# POLAR_SERVER=sandbox
# An organization access token of the sandbox org:
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=polar_oat_...
# The secret of a sandbox webhook endpoint pointing at a public tunnel to localhost, e.g.
# `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:8787` → https://<random>.trycloudflare.com/api/webhooks/polar
# (Polar has no local forwarding CLI; see docs/polar-migration/04-verification.md):
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# The sandbox credits product (one-time; each checkout sets its own USD price):
# POLAR_CREDITS_PRODUCT_ID=...
# The sandbox membership product (yearly; empty = no membership is sold), and the flag that charges it
# (off in wrangler.jsonc: without it nobody needs a membership, whatever is sold). Both set = power mode
# (and Canvas) on own keys and buying credit need a membership; Learn and spending held credit never do:
# POLAR_MEMBERSHIP_PRODUCT_ID=...
# ANNUAL_FEE_ENABLED=true
# A code that waives the membership fee for whoever enters it (empty = no code redemption):
# MEMBERSHIP_WAIVER_CODE=
# The markup is MARKUP_BPS (wrangler.jsonc).

# --- Option C: the built-in provider on credit, offline (no OpenRouter, no payments). Works with Option A or B.
# A fake built-in provider (Learn's Normal and Max tiers) that reports a fixed cost per call (the shape the worker tests use):
# SIMPLE_PROVIDER='{"id":"openrouter","kind":"fake","label":"Tangent","defaultModel":"simple","models":[{"id":"simple","label":"Normal","tier":"normal"},{"id":"smart","label":"Max","tier":"max"}],"options":{"chunkSize":4,"costUsd":0.001234}}'
# Placeholders so sends are allowed (top-ups and the membership checkout won't work with them;
# leave POLAR_MEMBERSHIP_PRODUCT_ID empty, or waive yourself with the README's SQL), or instead
# PERSONAL_CREDIT_ENABLED=true (below):
# POLAR_SERVER=sandbox
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=polar_oat_placeholder
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder
# Then grant yourself credit (5000000 = $5) with the SQL insert into credit_grants from the README
# ("Manual credit or adjustments", with --local; the account is `default_simple` under Option A,
# `u_<your user id>` under Option B, for both apps), then pick "Use Tangent credit" and chat at
# http://localhost:8787/learn/, or pick the "Tangent credit" provider in the power app.

# --- The community credit pool (docs/pool/SPEC.md); off in wrangler.jsonc. Its caps, price table
# and TTLs are the POOL_* vars there (parsed in src/config.ts). With Option C's fake provider,
# price its "simple" model so the pool can reserve for it:
# POOL_ENABLED=true
# POOL_MODEL=simple
# MODEL_PRICES='{"simple":{"in":100000,"out":400000,"context":131072}}'
# Learn then spends from the pool when it picks the pool, or when its credit runs out (sends only).
# Admin-granted personal credit without payments:
# PERSONAL_CREDIT_ENABLED=true
# Credit yourself as a purchase would, without a payment: POST /api/admin/credit with
# "mode": "simulated_purchase" (personal only; fund the pool with "target": "pool", "mode":
# "adjustment"; see the README's "Manual credit or adjustments"). Never in production.
# DEV_PURCHASES_ENABLED=true
